# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Multi-School Management System — dashboard (frontend/) environment
#
#  One variable, read in one place: `src/lib/apiClient.ts`.
#
#  NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle when `next build`
#  runs, so this must be set at BUILD time — in `.env.production` beside this
#  file, or in the shell that runs `npm run build`. Setting it when the server
#  starts (`next start`, or PM2's msms-web) changes nothing the browser sees.
#  Rebuild after changing it.
#
#  The value is the API's public origin plus its prefix — the host nginx serves
#  the API on (deploy/nginx/msms.conf, the :443 API block) and the backend's
#  API_PREFIX. The dashboard's own origin must be listed in the backend's
#  CORS_ORIGINS, and the two hostnames must share a registrable domain: the
#  session cookies are SameSite=Lax (see the note in deploy/nginx/msms.conf).
#
#  Unset, apiClient.ts falls back to http://localhost:4000/api/v1 — right for
#  `npm run dev` against a local backend, wrong everywhere else.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.msms.example.com/api/v1
